46s uptime with `NRestarts=0` — already past the 30s crash interval it was stuck in. The 150s watch is still running; I'll confirm when it lands.

## Applied and switched

`hosts/lucie/observability.nix`:

```nix
live_store = {
  wal.path = "${tempoDir}/live-store/traces";
  shutdown_marker_dir = "${tempoDir}/live-store/shutdown-marker";
};

block_builder.wal.path = "${tempoDir}/block-builder/traces";
backend_scheduler.local_work_path = "${tempoDir}/scheduler";
```

Before → after:

| | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| `NRestarts` | ticking every ~30s (848 on the previous boot) | `0` |
| `/ready` | never bound | `HTTP 200 ready` |
| ports | none | 32040, 32317 (OTLP gRPC), 34218 (OTLP HTTP) all listening |
| `/var/tempo` | `mkdir: read-only file system` | never created |
| `/var/lib/tempo` | empty | `live-store/ traces/ wal/` |

Two notes on the switch itself:

- `nixos-rebuild switch` exited 4, but from `nix-serve-tunnel.service` (`ssh ... status=255/EXCEPTION`) — that was already failing before my change, unrelated to tempo. Worth a look separately if you care about the binary cache tunnel.
- `otlpHttpPort = 34218` still breaks your `32xxx` pattern. It works, it's just the odd one out if `32318` was the intent.

The nightly build guards from issue #9 are still unapplied — that timer fires again in ~19 hours.

